To add emphasis to his argument, he invited attention of the court to - (i) order dated 25.02.2002, whereby the anticipatory bail application of the family members of the respondent-husband was dismissed;
(ii) anticipatory bail application no.27/2002 filed by the respondent in Complaint Case No.577/2001 under Section 498A/504/406 IPC; (iii) reply filed by the respondent in maintenance N.C. No.
2023:DHC:2686-DB Case No.27/2001 before the Chief Judicial Magistrate, Madhepura; and (iv) an order dated 16.09.2002 passed by High Court of Patna in Crl.Misc.No.12273/2002 on an application for grant of anticipatory bail in complaint case under Section 498A/504/406 IPC, which contains reference to the proceedings of divorce pending at Delhi.
